     3	/// The Color sub-tab's **Qualifier** section (spec §11 GR-13, grading-2
     4	/// G2-4), on adjustment clips only, after Adjustment: which of the pixels
     5	/// behind the clip its grade reaches.
     6	///
     7	/// Per range two rows — its checkbox (Hue, Saturation, Luma) in the label
     8	/// column then its strip (`RangeStripControl`), then three captioned fields
     9	/// (Centre, Width, Soft in whole degrees; Low, High, Soft to two decimals) —
    10	/// then Invert, then Blur (spec §11 GR-35: the house slider and field,
    11	/// 0–100 %, one step "Qualifier Blur"), then Pick from Canvas and the Show
    12	/// Selection switch, both sent to the editor as commands
    13	/// (`EditorViewController+Qualifier.swift`, `+Seeing`). A checkbox writes
    14	/// `{}` or `null` (one step named after the range); a strip drag is the live trio; a field one commit; each sends the
    15	/// WHOLE range to every selected clip, the first clip's values being the
    16	/// ones shown (the mixed badge says when the others differ). Every row
    17	/// writes `video.qualifier`, so a keyed action marks them all as one key.
    18	extension VideoPane {
