| **Remove from action N** | The selected action animates the row | Takes the row out of the action. |
| **Go to action M** | The row shows ◇ | Selects the action that animates the row, and moves the playhead to that action's end. |
| **Set end value to default** | An action is selected, and the row has a default and can animate | Sets the value at the action's end to the row's default. |
| **Reset to default** | Any other row with a default | Puts the row back to its default. |

The two default items are greyed while the row already holds its default.

**Set end value to default** and **Remove from action N** aren't the same. The first makes the clip animate to the default. The second stops the action touching the row.

## Good to know
| [Qualifier](/color/qualifiers/), on an adjustment clip | Each range's numbers. **Invert** and turning a range on or off switch at the end |
Ticking **Hue**, **Saturation** or **Luma** with an action selected turns that range on at the action's end. It has nothing to ramp from, so it stays off through the action and then appears whole, at the end values you set. **Invert** switches at the end too.

If the clip has no qualifier at all when the action starts, the whole qualifier appears at the action's end, and its **Blur** doesn't ramp either.

An action can't turn off a range the clip already has on. Unticking a box with an action selected only takes that range back out of the action. To turn a range off, press <kbd>Esc</kbd> and untick it on the clip.

- A path is `"group.key"`, with a group of `video`, `audio` or `text` and one of its top-level keys, such as `video.shadow`, `text.width` or `audio.limiter`.
- One deeper path exists: `audio.eq.<slot>` switches that EQ slot off. The slots are `high_pass`, `low_shelf`, `band_1`, `band_2`, `band_3`, `high_shelf` and `low_pass`.
- Only optional keys can go off. A required key such as `video.opacity` is refused.
- A path can't also be named in `patch`.
- `graphic` paths are refused: name the value a prop ends at in `patch`.
- `video.cutout` is refused: `set_video` with `{cutout: null}` removes a cutout.
- `video.motion`, `video.hide_silent` and `text.words` are refused here too.
- **Turning a qualifier range on** switches at the action's end. An action can't turn off a range the clip has on: unticking it with an action selected only takes the range back out of the action.
*Agents:* `add_action`, then `set_action_end` with a `video` patch carrying `color`, `wheels`, `curves`, `look.amount` or `qualifier`.
Unchecking a switch inside an action (a shadow or an outline, for example) turns that property off when the action ends.

